  "preamble": "The complete loss or elision of the voiceless bilabial plosive /p/, a characteristic sound change in the history of Celtic languages and various other lineages. Initial *p was also lost in Australian initial-dropping languages, such as Uradhi anga- < Proto-Paman *panga- 'dig' and Arrernte al- < *pula 'they (dual)'.",
